menu "Configuration"
	depends on PACKAGE_netsukuku-rs

config NETSUKUKU_RS_UPX
	bool "Compress the ntkd binary with UPX (--best --lzma)"
	default y
	help
	  Shrinks the installed ntkd binary from ~3.90 MiB to ~1.21 MiB at the cost of a one-time
	  ~69ms self-decompression on every start. Worthwhile here because flash is the scarce
	  resource on most OpenWrt targets and ntkd is a long-running daemon that pays that cost
	  once, not per-request. Disable this only if `upx` is unavailable for your target
	  architecture on the build host, or if you specifically need the binary's pages to be
	  demand-paged (a UPX image cannot be, so the full decompressed binary stays resident
	  instead of only the pages actually touched) rather than flash-optimal.

endmenu
